## How to JOIN tables and identify primary and foreign keys 
## LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN, INNER JOIN 
## 1. Understand your anchor table and set it as left table, then primary keys come from that 
## 2. When writing the code 
##    FROM sales             |  it means sales left join customer, so sales is the anchor table and customer 
##    LEFT JOIN customer     |  will join matching rows 
##    FROM customer          |  this produces the same table as LEFT JOIN but in reverse order, customer right joins sales 
##    RIGHT JOIN sales       |  so sales is the anchor table still and customer joins the matching rows 
##      ON sales.cust_id = customer.cust_id  | since sales is the anchor then sales.cust_id is the primary key 
##    focus on join (inner join) and left join 
##    FROM sales                                   |   the anchor table is customer because sales joins on the right, so 
##    JOIN customer                                |   primary key is customer.cust_id 
##      ON customer.cust_id = sales.cust_id        |
